   "seriesAdminGuidance": [
    "AAFP recommends persons aged 65 years and older preferentially receive any one of the following high-dose, adjuvanted or recombinant, or mRNA influenza vaccines: trivalent high-dose inactivated influenza vaccine (HD-IIV3), trivalent recombinant influenza vaccine (RIV3), trivalent adjuvanted inactivated influenza vaccine (aIIV3) or Influenza, mRNA, trivalent, PF (mRNA). If none of these three vaccines is available at an opportunity for vaccine administration, then any other age-appropriate influenza vaccine should be used.",
    "All persons aged 6 months and older with egg allergy should receive influenza vaccine. Any influenza vaccine (egg based or non-egg based) that is otherwise appropriate for the recipient's age and health status can be used.",
    "Solid organ transplant (SOT) recipients aged 19 through 64 years receiving immunosuppressive medications can receive HD-IIV3 or aIIV3. No preference over other age-appropriate IIV3 or RIV3 vaccines. Refer to IDSA for the recommend timing and spacing of vaccination surrounding SOT and other immunocompromised groups.",
    "AAFP recommends non-pregnant, immunocompetent persons over the age of 19 receive vaccination between September and October. Those over the age of 65 should avoid vaccination in July-August unless later vaccination may not be feasible.",
    "ACOG recommends individuals who are or will be pregnant during influenza season receive an appropriate, seasonally updated influenza vaccine at any time during pregnancy.",
    "AAP recommends vaccine should be offered to those under the age of 18 as soon as it becomes available, especially to\nthose recommended to receive 2 doses. The recommended dose(s) ideally should be received by\nthe end of October."
